---
title: Frequently Asked Questions
description: Common questions about FOSSBilling, BoxBilling, and everything in between.
---

## What is FOSSBilling?

FOSSBilling is a free, open-source billing and client management platform for hosting providers, domain resellers, and digital service businesses.

### Is this BoxBilling?

**No.** FOSSBilling was created in 2022 as a fork of BoxBilling, which had become unmaintained and had numerous security vulnerabilities.

| | BoxBilling | FOSSBilling |
|---|---|---|
| **Status** | Unmaintained | Actively developed |
| **Security** | Multiple known vulnerabilities | Regular security updates |
| **PHP Support** | 7.4 & 8.0 (outdated) | [8.2–8.4](/getting-started/requirements#version) |
| **Avg. Vulnerability Fix** | 71 days | 6 days |
| **Translations** | Outdated, error-prone | Plural support, auto language detection, improved localization |
| **Security Features** | Minimal | Session protection, HTTPS-only mode, CSRF protection, and more |

The team tried to revive BoxBilling but couldn't due to ownership issues. FOSSBilling was created to provide a dependable, truly open-source alternative.

## Is FOSSBilling production-ready?

**Short answer:** Not yet, but getting closer.

We're actively fixing bugs, improving security, and replacing inherited legacy systems. FOSSBilling is much more stable and secure than the final BoxBilling releases, but it is still moving toward a 1.0 milestone.

**If you use it in production:**
- Stick to [stable releases](https://fossbilling.org/downloads) or [GitHub releases](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/releases)
- Avoid preview/pre-release commits unless they fix a specific issue
- Always back up and test in staging first
- Expect potential breaking changes before 1.0

Track progress on our [roadmap](https://github.com/orgs/FOSSBilling/projects/2/views/8).

## When will [feature] be added?

We'd love FOSSBilling to do everything, but right now we're focused on **stability, security, and getting the basics right.**

If you need something specific:
- Check [existing feature requests](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/issues?q=is:open+is:issue+label:"feature+request")
- [Submit a new request](https://fossbilling.org/feature-request)
- Consider [building it yourself](/developing-fossbilling/) — we welcome contributions!
- Ask in the community — someone might build it

### Why doesn't FOSSBilling have [feature] that WHMCS has?

Two reasons:

1. **We're not trying to be WHMCS.** Popular doesn't mean right for everyone.
2. **Resources.** WHMCS is a 20+ year old commercial product with paid developers. FOSSBilling is volunteer-run with a small community. We move at a different pace.

## Does FOSSBilling work with Pterodactyl?

**No, and we have no plans to add support.**

The community is welcome to build a Pterodactyl integration. See [our stance](/server-managers/others#pterodactyl) for details.

## Is FOSSBilling free?

**Yes — completely.**

FOSS stands for **F**ree and **O**pen-**S**ource **S**oftware. You can use, study, modify, and distribute it freely. The core software will always be free.

Third parties *can* sell commercial modules/extensions, but the base FOSSBilling software is and will remain free.

## How can I contribute?

Open source lives or dies by community involvement. Every contribution helps:

- **Code** — Fix bugs, add features
- **Documentation** — Help improve these docs
- **Testing** — Try preview releases, report issues
- **Community** — Answer questions, help others
- **Financial** — [Sponsor the project](/faq#how-can-i-sponsor-or-donate)

See [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) for details.

## How can I sponsor or donate?

- [GitHub Sponsors](https://github.com/sponsors/FOSSBilling)
- [Open Collective](https://opencollective.com/fossbilling)

Funds go to:
- Software licenses and tools
- Hosting infrastructure
- Development bounties for specific tasks

All expenses are [publicly visible](https://opencollective.com/fossbilling).

## Something's not working. What should I do?

1. Check the [Troubleshooting guide](/troubleshooting/)
2. Search [Discord](https://fossbilling.org/discord) for your issue
3. Ask in Discord if you can't find an answer
4. If it's a bug, [open a GitHub issue](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/issues)

Most issues are server configuration problems (especially `.htaccess` or NGINX config), not bugs in FOSSBilling itself.

## Where are the logs?

FOSSBilling stores logs under `/data/log/`:

- `php_error.log` — PHP errors and general logging
- Additional directories for specific channels (rotated daily, 90 days retention)

## Does FOSSBilling support IPv6-only environments?

Partially, with caveats:

- **Automatic updates** — Uses GitHub, which doesn't support IPv6. Workaround: [IPv6 GitHub proxy](https://danwin1210.de/github-ipv6-proxy.php)
- **Error reporting** — Uses Sentry, which doesn't support IPv6 yet (they're working on it)
